CoolSchool ships dedicated eSpeak language packs so DE / FR / EN / RO
prompts are pronounced with that language’s phoneme rules, even when the
browser only has English SpeechSynthesis voices.

Vendored engine (web/tts/mespeak.js, mespeak-core.js) and voice JSON
(web/tts/voices/{de,fr,ro}.json, voices/en/en.json):

  meSpeak.js (Modular eSpeak) — Norbert Landsteiner / mass:werk
  https://www.masswerk.at/mespeak
  based on speak.js (https://github.com/kripken/speak.js)
  and eSpeak (https://espeak.sourceforge.net / eSpeak NG)

These files are licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.
See COPYING in this directory. The rest of CoolSchool is unchanged;
this folder is the GPL TTS engine plus four language voice packages.

FR / RO voice JSON still uses the vendored eSpeak dictionaries from
meSpeak (`dict` field). Only the small `voice` text blob was edited:
female formant / pitch-range profile, no echo, no breath, no Klatt
variant. That text is the same eSpeak voice-file format (GPL-3) as the
original male `fr` / `ro` packs. No MBROLA or third-party voice
database was added.
